; worldback.eval — a dungeon with TWO ways in (Michael, 2026-09-09).
;
; The front gate and the back way open the SAME dungeon from different places
; on the world map, and land in different parts of it. What this is really
; checking is that the two are not secretly one:
;
;   - the back way lands on level2 at 9,4, NOT on showcase's start cell;
;   - walking out of the FRONT exit surfaces at the front location even though
;     the party came in by the back — an exit knows its own door;
;   - coming out of a door DISCOVERS it, which is how a back way is found from
;     the inside.
logecho on
reset
leave

; --- in by the BACK way: a different level, a different cell -----------------
discover waystation_back
enter waystation_back
state
mapinfo
pos
world

; --- out by the FRONT: a different door than the one we came in by -----------
leave waystation
world
